I made some other test : 

- if I set env var `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0` on my machine, it works (but it's a very ugly workaroud).

- if I set env var `NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=C:\certs\Company-ROOT-CA-2023.crt`, it doesn't works on podman desktop, but it works when I execute my demo code : 
```ts
import { Octokit } from "@octokit/rest";

const octokit = new Octokit();

async function getLatestDockerComposeRelease() {
    try {
        // Récupérer les releases du dépôt Docker Compose
        const { data } = await octokit.rest.repos.listReleases({
            owner: "docker",
            repo: "compose",
        });

        // Filtrer pour trouver la dernière release pour Windows
        const latestRelease = data.find(release => 
            release.assets.some(asset => asset.name.includes("windows"))
        );

        if (latestRelease) {
            console.log(`last Docker Compose for Windows : ${latestRelease.tag_name}`);
            console.log(`release note : ${latestRelease.body}`);
            console.log(`download here : ${latestRelease.assets.find(asset => asset.name.includes("windows"))?.browser_download_url}`);
        } else {
            console.log("no version found.");
        }
    } catch (error) {
        console.error("Error :", error);
    }
}

getLatestDockerComposeRelease();
```

Have you an idea why NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED has effect and NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS does not ?

I ran some other tests with my demo.ts and saw these things.

It works without any environment variables if I do this:
- Use node-fetch instead of the built-in fetch
- set the global agent options CA
- configure fetch for requests on Octokit.

```ts
import { Octokit } from "@octokit/rest";
import fetch from "node-fetch"  // <- use node-fetch

import { globalAgent } from 'https'
import { getCACertificates } from 'node:tls'

globalAgent.options.ca = getCACertificates('system') // <- configure certificate

const octokit = new Octokit({
    request: {
      fetch, // <- configure fetch like you did in your PR
    },
  });

async function getLatestDockerComposeRelease() {
    try {
        const { data } = await octokit.rest.repos.listReleases({
            owner: "docker",
            repo: "compose",
        });

        const latestRelease = data.find(release => 
            release.assets.some(asset => asset.name.includes("windows"))
        );

        if (latestRelease) {
            console.log(`last Docker Compose for Windows : ${latestRelease.tag_name}`);
            console.log(`release note : ${latestRelease.body}`);
            console.log(`download here : ${latestRelease.assets.find(asset => asset.name.includes("windows"))?.browser_download_url}`);
        } else {
            console.log("no version found.");
        }
    } catch (error) {
        console.error("Error :", error);
    }
}

await getLatestDockerComposeRelease();
```
